---
import ContentLayout from '@/layouts/content-layout.astro'
import { MvpCostEstimator } from '@/components/mvp-cost-estimator'
import {
	AI_ASSIST_FACTOR,
	AI_FEATURE_THRESHOLD,
	BASELINE_POLISH_HOURS,
	FEATURE_COUNT_THRESHOLD,
	FEATURES,
	HOURLY_RATE_RANGE,
	HOURS_PER_BILLABLE_WEEK,
	INTERACTION_RULES,
	MINIMUM_PROJECT_PRICE,
} from '@/lib/mvp-estimator'
import { formatUsd } from '@/lib/pricing'

const [rateMin, rateMax] = HOURLY_RATE_RANGE

// Average build-time saving across the whole feature catalog, weighted by hours.
const preAiHours = FEATURES.reduce((sum, f) => sum + f.minHours + f.maxHours, 0)
const aiHours = FEATURES.reduce((sum, f) => sum + (f.minHours + f.maxHours) * AI_ASSIST_FACTOR[f.category], 0)
const aiSavingPercent = Math.round((1 - aiHours / preAiHours) * 100)
---

<ContentLayout
	title="App & Software Development Cost Calculator | ilzam.dev"
	description="Free app and software development cost calculator. Tick the features your product needs and get a price range and week-by-week timeline. No signup."
	wide
>
	<h1 class="text-3xl font-light leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-4xl print:hidden">
		App &amp; Software Development Cost Calculator
	</h1>
	<p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground print:hidden">
		Find out roughly what your app or software product will cost to build, and how
		long it takes. Tick the features you need and the price and timeline update
		instantly. No signup, and no technical knowledge needed: each feature comes
		with a short explanation.
	</p>

	<div class="mt-8">
		<MvpCostEstimator client:load />
	</div>

	<section class="mt-16 max-w-3xl print:hidden">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How this estimate is calculated</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Each feature has a typical range of hours it takes to build. The calculator
			adds up the features you tick, then adjusts for a few things that change the
			real cost.
		</p>
		<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">{FEATURES.length} common features</strong>, grouped
				into the categories above, from user accounts and payments to AI and mobile apps.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">Built with AI in 2026.</strong> Building with AI tools is
				now standard practice, and it cuts build time by about {aiSavingPercent}% on average
				compared with a few years ago. The saving is biggest for routine work like screens, forms,
				and admin panels, and smallest for payments and connections to other tools, where every
				detail still has to be checked by hand.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">Features that depend on each other.</strong> Some
				combinations take extra work. For example, company accounts plus subscriptions
				means billing each company per seat. The calculator checks for
				{INTERACTION_RULES.length} of these combinations.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">Bigger products take longer to test.</strong> Picking
				{AI_FEATURE_THRESHOLD} or more AI features, or {FEATURE_COUNT_THRESHOLD} or more features in
				total, adds time, because every new piece can affect the others.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">Launch.</strong> Every project includes
				{BASELINE_POLISH_HOURS[0]} to {BASELINE_POLISH_HOURS[1]} hours of final testing and going live.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">Price.</strong> Total hours multiplied by
				{rateMin === rateMax ? formatUsd(rateMin) : `${formatUsd(rateMin)} to ${formatUsd(rateMax)}`} per hour,
				with a minimum of {formatUsd(MINIMUM_PROJECT_PRICE)} for any project.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong class="text-foreground">Timeline.</strong> Based on {HOURS_PER_BILLABLE_WEEK} hours
				of focused work a week, which leaves time for calls, reviews, and your feedback.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Use the result as a ballpark for budgeting. A fixed quote needs a short call,
			because the biggest cost drivers are things a checklist can't capture:
			connecting to systems you already use, rules you have to follow (for example,
			handling health or financial data), and how polished the first version needs
			to be.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Why not a bigger AI saving? Writing code got much faster, but checking it did not. Google's
			<a href="https://blog.google/technology/developers/dora-report-2025/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">2025 DORA research</a>
			found that about 90% of software professionals now use AI, and that it magnifies a team's
			existing strengths and weaknesses. That's why the testing and launch time in this calculator
			is not reduced.
		</p>
	</section>
</ContentLayout>
